CORE
main.cpp
--cpp20 --object-bits 11 --no-unwinding-assertions
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ inheriting constructor sets the flag: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ inheriting constructor forwards the value: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
[namespace.udecl]/2 + [class.inhctor.init]: an inheriting constructor
declaration (`using Base::Base;`) inherits the base's constructor *templates*
as well.  Fixed by registering the base's constructor-template ids in the
derived class's scope under the derived name (so overload resolution finds and
instantiates them, initializing the base subobject) and by recording that the
class has inherited constructors so it is not treated as an aggregate
([dcl.init.aggr]/1, C++17).  Cross-checked against g++ and clang++.
